Carried from pingdotgg/t3code PR #36029, "fix(server): an idle Claude thread now wakes when its background command
finishes" (https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code/pull/36029), head 5cc2e2a439, diffed against its merge base with main
(4860a73069). Applies to v0.1.12 as is.

Changed from upstream: only the PR's test file is left out (ClaudeAdapterV2.test.ts: four cases, the probe returning
false after the notification; it runs in upstream's CI, not in this build). The source change is upstream's, byte for
byte: hasPendingBackgroundWork also holds the session while a remembered native thread has an owed wake task, so T3
no longer closes the Claude process between Claude's task_notification and the wake turn Claude starts for it (seen
here as "No response requested." right after a <task-notification>; ~/agents/improve/raw/dropped-wakes-2026-11-25.txt).
Checked against 0.1.12: releaseIfStillIdle and the orchestrator's detach probe still release through this probe.

Replace with upstream: as soon as a T3 release includes #36029 (no adaptation to compare).

